node_modules/
dist/
.DS_Store
*.log
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.wrangler/
coverage/
.aider*
!.aider.conf.yml
!.aider.model.settings.yml
!.aiderignore
.claude/tmp/
.claude/settings.local.json

# `bun run shapes:still` writes whatever was last asked for — one body, one
# skin, or every skin — so its content is a question somebody asked rather than
# a state of the tree. Committing it would be pure churn.
tools/shape-sheet/skin-sheet.svg

# `bun run frames` writes its PNGs here, one directory per sha. A picture taken
# to show the owner something is a question somebody asked rather than a state
# of the tree — and until it was ignored, every lane that took one could not
# land, because `git status --porcelain` counts untracked files.
docs/frames/

# `bun run probe` answers a question about a running world, and the script that
# asks one is a throwaway — the finding it exists for is that such a file had
# nowhere to live, so it needs a place nobody has to remember to sweep. The
# directory itself stays, by its `.gitkeep`; what a session drops in it does not.
tools/probe/scratch/*
!tools/probe/scratch/.gitkeep
